{
  "subtype": "faceted_decomposition",
  "concept": "praise_and_complaint_drivers",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "primary_domain",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "irrelevant",
      "rationale": "Product category is context/segmentation, not a driver aspect of praise or complaint. It classifies WHAT is reviewed, not WHY it is praised or criticized."
    },
    {
      "name": "quality_or_durability_issue",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Product quality/durability is a genuine constitutive aspect of what drives complaints (and its absence, praise)."
    },
    {
      "name": "works_as_intended",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Functional performance / whether the product works is a core aspect of praise/complaint drivers, distinct from build quality."
    },
    {
      "name": "value_for_money",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Price/value is a legitimate constitutive dimension driving satisfaction and dissatisfaction."
    },
    {
      "name": "expectation_alignment",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Whether the product met/exceeded/fell short of expectations is a facet of drivers, though it partly overlaps with performance and value as a summary judgment."
    },
    {
      "name": "recommendation_stance",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "restatement",
      "rationale": "Recommend vs discourage is an OUTCOME/summary of overall sentiment, essentially restating the praise/complaint valence rather than a constitutive driver of it."
    }
  ],
  "facet_columns": [
    "quality_or_durability_issue",
    "works_as_intended",
    "value_for_money",
    "expectation_alignment"
  ],
  "non_facet_columns": [
    "primary_domain",
    "recommendation_stance"
  ],
  "mutual_exclusivity": 0.6,
  "exhaustiveness": 0.55,
  "rationale": "Four of six columns are true facets of the drivers concept: quality/durability, functional performance, value, and expectation alignment. However mutual exclusivity is imperfect because expectation_alignment is a composite summary that overlaps with performance and value, and works_as_intended vs quality_or_durability_issue partly co-vary. primary_domain is segmentation (irrelevant to drivers) and recommendation_stance restates the overall praise/complaint outcome rather than decomposing its drivers. Exhaustiveness is moderate: important driver facets like customer service/shipping/seller experience, usability/ease of use, aesthetics, and content/subjective enjoyment (highly relevant given book/music/movie dominance) are absent, so the set does not fully cover the concept's constitutive aspects."
}

